1
00:00:04,580 --> 00:00:07,840
Ryo-san, speaking of which,
Valentine's Day is coming up soon, isn't it.

2
00:00:07,920 --> 00:00:09,780
What's Valentine's Day to me?

3
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:11,337
That thing, you see,

4
00:00:11,387 --> 00:00:17,620
is some worthless custom a candy shop
owner dreamed up just to sell chocolate.

5
00:00:17,980 --> 00:00:21,360
Right, it's a day that has
nothing to do with you, Ryo-san.

6
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:26,860
Argh! I want chocolate too!
Somebody give me some!

7
00:00:33,140 --> 00:00:37,080
When you watch TV, brighten the room
and sit back from the screen, okay?

8
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:50,220
Anyone with no money, come to me!

9
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:54,940
I've got none either, but don't worry.

10
00:00:54,940 --> 00:01:08,860
Look, blue skies, white clouds,
somehow it'll all work out in the end.

11
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:25,880
Anyone without a job, come to me!

12
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:30,460
I don't have one either, so don't you worry.

13
00:01:30,460 --> 00:01:37,540
Look, even the burning steel

14
00:01:39,240 --> 00:01:44,220
will somehow work out in the end.

15
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:49,500
You understand, right?
Yeah, yeah, I understand.

16
00:01:49,500 --> 00:01:53,380
Once you understand, shut up and follow me!

17
00:02:14,060 --> 00:02:15,440
Time really flies, doesn't it.

18
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:17,920
It's already the 21st century

19
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:20,220
What's with the sudden talk?

20
00:02:20,220 --> 00:02:22,920
When I was a kid, in the 21st century,

21
00:02:22,920 --> 00:02:26,540
I thought all cars would
be running through tubes.

22
00:02:26,540 --> 00:02:28,660
I've seen that too, you know.

23
00:02:33,500 --> 00:02:40,500
But in reality, cars still crawl along the ground,
sharing the same roads as pedestrians.

24
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:44,660
With things like this, traffic accidents
won't disappear anytime soon, will they?

25
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:50,620
Couldn't cars at least become more futuristic,
so accidents absolutely can't happen?

26
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:57,560
Senpai, I found a bicycle that
definitely won't cause any accidents!

27
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:58,400
What?

28
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:58,600
What?

29
00:03:01,320 --> 00:03:04,240
A big rearview mirror that
lets you see far behind,

30
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:07,620
turn signals that can't possibly be missed,

31
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:09,940
and training wheels to prevent tipping over.

32
00:03:10,320 --> 00:03:13,100
It's even wearing protective gear.

33
00:03:13,100 --> 00:03:17,140
Going that far almost seems like
it might be more dangerous, though.

34
00:03:17,880 --> 00:03:21,260
I feel like I've seen that
bicycle somewhere before.

35
00:03:21,640 --> 00:03:22,320
Really?

36
00:03:23,075 --> 00:03:27,800
It feels like it's sealed away together
with some memory I'd rather not recall.

37
00:03:31,080 --> 00:03:32,980
They're going, senpai!

38
00:03:32,980 --> 00:03:35,360
Something about it bugs me. Let's follow it.

39
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:40,560
I'm home.

40
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:46,381
You look like this family's kid,

41
00:03:46,431 --> 00:03:47,620
Tetsuo Ohara is

42
00:03:47,620 --> 00:03:49,352
No, it's Tetsuo Ohara,

43
00:03:49,402 --> 00:03:51,780
this is Chief Ohara's house.

44
00:03:53,460 --> 00:03:58,060
Tetsuo Ohara is a police officer assigned
to the Katsushika station's traffic division.

45
00:03:58,720 --> 00:04:04,100
He's normally quiet,
but when the talk turns to traffic safety,

46
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:07,920
he becomes a demon for traffic safety.

47
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:12,900
He transforms into the Ohara-style
Traffic Safety Instructor, Part 7!

48
00:04:18,580 --> 00:04:21,340
The demon of traffic safety returns!

49
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:25,460
I once received traffic safety
instruction from him too,

50
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:27,240
and went through a terrible ordeal.

51
00:04:27,240 --> 00:04:29,680
You mean Chief Ohara?

52
00:04:29,680 --> 00:04:33,580
I knew I'd seen that
bicycle somewhere before.

53
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:36,100
It looks exactly like Chief
Ohara's white police motorcycle.

54
00:04:36,100 --> 00:04:39,200
What business do you have with my son?

55
00:04:39,620 --> 00:04:41,220
The Dance of Yankip.

56
00:04:44,140 --> 00:04:45,580
The art of flag-making.

57
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:53,320
And who might you be?

58
00:04:54,200 --> 00:04:55,380
Sorry, sorry.

59
00:04:55,380 --> 00:04:57,860
I was told some strange
man was following you,

60
00:04:57,860 --> 00:04:59,400
so I thought it might be a kidnapping.

61
00:05:01,120 --> 00:05:02,040
One-way street.

62
00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:04,080
Come here and apologize too.

63
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:04,760
Yes, sir.

64
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,200
One-way street.

65
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:08,700
I'm sorry.

66
00:05:09,620 --> 00:05:11,640
One-way street... don't tell me that's -

67
00:05:11,640 --> 00:05:12,920
That child's name?

68
00:05:12,920 --> 00:05:15,840
We have six sons in our house, you see.

69
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:18,498
The eldest is Right Turn, then Left Turn,

70
00:05:18,548 --> 00:05:20,518
Straight Ahead, One-Way Street,

71
00:05:20,568 --> 00:05:21,763
No Parking,

72
00:05:21,813 --> 00:05:24,800
and then Lane Direction Designation.

73
00:05:24,800 --> 00:05:26,800
What incredible names.

74
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:30,060
The names are impressive, but wait
till you see the inside of the house.

75
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:35,040
Traffic regulations must
be learned from a young age.

76
00:05:35,040 --> 00:05:39,920
That's why we've put road signs
in every corner of the house.

77
00:05:44,200 --> 00:05:46,040
I see, you're really thorough.

78
00:05:46,980 --> 00:05:48,380
Excuse me for a moment.

79
00:05:52,320 --> 00:05:54,540
Is this a retail-only model?

80
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:58,440
Sorry to keep you waiting.

81
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:01,500
You really do change drastically, don't you?

82
00:06:04,860 --> 00:06:05,820
That...

83
00:06:06,640 --> 00:06:09,300
Isn't that the police light
that was on top of that helmet?

84
00:06:09,920 --> 00:06:11,480
Is it really that important to you?

85
00:06:12,540 --> 00:06:17,960
It's what inspired me to take
up the path of traffic safety.

86
00:06:18,940 --> 00:06:20,960
It's embarrassing to say, but...

87
00:06:20,960 --> 00:06:25,620
You see,
I used to be the leader of the Raizoku.

88
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:27,020
Raizoku?

89
00:06:27,280 --> 00:06:29,160
The old biker gang.

90
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:31,420
We were called the Black Meteor.

91
00:06:33,340 --> 00:06:34,960
Sounds like you were a real troublemaker.

92
00:06:34,960 --> 00:06:38,080
I committed every traffic
violation there was.

93
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:41,540
I was confident I
wouldn't cause an accident.

94
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:45,080
Because I had complete
faith in my own technique.

95
00:06:47,080 --> 00:06:48,620
But then one day...

96
00:06:53,860 --> 00:06:57,120
The police car that was chasing us

97
00:06:57,120 --> 00:06:59,020
ended up causing an accident.

98
00:07:04,120 --> 00:07:06,560
For a while now, they've been trying hard

99
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:09,560
to reform us. It was that policeman.

100
00:07:10,580 --> 00:07:11,220
Old man.

101
00:07:11,220 --> 00:07:16,040
Look, traffic violations are not okay.

102
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:20,040
Even if you're fine,
it causes trouble for everyone around you.

103
00:07:20,040 --> 00:07:22,680
Okay, okay, I get it. Now stop talking.

104
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:24,880
I'll never commit

105
00:07:24,880 --> 00:07:27,340
another traffic violation.
I swear on this police light.

106
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:29,400
Old man.

107
00:07:29,400 --> 00:07:30,780
Hey, old man!

108
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:35,000
After that, I became a police officer.

109
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:39,360
Taking up the old man's cause, I set out to wipe
traffic violations off the face of the earth.

110
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:42,360
So you're carrying on that man's will.

111
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:44,980
So it's a keepsake patrol light, is it?

112
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:48,700
No, he's over ninety now
and still going strong!

113
00:07:48,700 --> 00:07:52,180
But his comrades wouldn't keep quiet.

114
00:07:52,180 --> 00:07:54,680
Especially the sub-leader, Watanuki.

115
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:57,720
After that,
he kept relentlessly stalking me.

116
00:07:58,520 --> 00:08:00,320
What is he doing now?

117
00:08:00,320 --> 00:08:04,500
Well, one day he suddenly
vanished without a trace.

118
00:08:04,500 --> 00:08:07,360
Rumor has it he went abroad, though.

119
00:08:10,680 --> 00:08:13,020
Looks like the eldest son has come home.

120
00:08:13,740 --> 00:08:15,980
That engine sound...
it's a Porsche, isn't it?

121
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:18,400
Hey, that doesn't match the image!

122
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:21,300
I just love the stubborn
craftsmanship of Porsches.

123
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:24,640
This house didn't have a garage, did it?

124
00:08:24,640 --> 00:08:26,860
Don't tell me you're planning
to park on the street!

125
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:30,200
Of course I wouldn't do something like that.

126
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:32,920
It stopped.

127
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,740
Dad, I'm home.

128
00:08:37,760 --> 00:08:39,420
Welcome back, right turn.

129
00:08:39,420 --> 00:08:42,600
W-why are you coming out of the closet?

130
00:08:42,600 --> 00:08:44,980
That's our family garage.

131
00:08:44,980 --> 00:08:47,400
There's no parking lot nearby, so...

132
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:50,440
What amazing safety equipment!

133
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:54,500
Since you've come all this way,
let me give you a ride.

134
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:57,000
Please wait just a moment.

135
00:09:00,560 --> 00:09:01,620
Could it be...?

136
00:09:02,260 --> 00:09:05,860
Known as a walking traffic law for 35 years.

137
00:09:07,360 --> 00:09:10,900
Ishido Shigan, seventh dan,
Ishizuru Tetsuo Kenzō

138
00:09:10,900 --> 00:09:12,660
Just as I thought, that's the look.

139
00:09:12,660 --> 00:09:14,920
I'm bringing the car out, so wait outside.

140
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:19,540
There doesn't seem to
be an entrance, though.

141
00:09:19,540 --> 00:09:21,280
How do you plan to get it out?

142
00:09:24,080 --> 00:09:25,040
What?

143
00:09:25,040 --> 00:09:28,900
Look, you're standing in front of the garage,
that's dangerous!

144
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:31,080
Which one's the dangerous one?!

145
00:09:31,080 --> 00:09:34,100
This part is rubber.
It's like passing through a wall!

146
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:39,100
Make sure to fasten the
32-point seatbelt properly.

147
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:40,700
This is what's such a hassle.

148
00:09:43,900 --> 00:09:45,740
It's a comfortable ride, isn't it.

149
00:09:45,740 --> 00:09:48,300
But what's that plate under the accelerator?

150
00:09:48,300 --> 00:09:50,820
So the speed can't go over 50 km/h.

151
00:09:50,820 --> 00:09:53,080
I've fitted a stopper.

152
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,940
Feels like it's more dangerous, though.

153
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:56,260
Mm-hm.

154
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:02,080
What's wrong all of a sudden?

155
00:10:02,080 --> 00:10:04,420
The traffic light is
hidden by the street trees.

156
00:10:04,960 --> 00:10:05,900
Indeed.

157
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:08,140
Where are you going?

158
00:10:08,140 --> 00:10:09,660
Wait here a moment.

159
00:10:09,660 --> 00:10:10,100
Yes.

160
00:10:10,960 --> 00:10:12,940
I know, about the street trees.

161
00:10:12,940 --> 00:10:16,360
As expected of Traffic
Safety Instructors' Squad 7.

162
00:10:18,400 --> 00:10:23,380
Lately, there are many places where street
trees block the traffic lights like that.

163
00:10:23,380 --> 00:10:28,080
Planting more greenery is fine,
but we also need to consider traffic safety.

164
00:10:28,080 --> 00:10:29,000
Indeed.

165
00:10:32,080 --> 00:10:35,800
Now what?
The crosswalk is nearly faded away.

166
00:10:35,800 --> 00:10:48,300
Do you do this every time you get in a car?

167
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:50,840
We should do it whenever we notice, right?

168
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:53,740
If we don't, and an accident happens,
we'll regret it.

169
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:54,320
That's right.

170
00:10:57,660 --> 00:10:58,720
Accidents

171
00:10:59,200 --> 00:11:04,300
This intersection has always had frequent accidents.
It's a flawed intersection.

172
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:09,200
I've been submitting opinions to higher-ups,
but nothing's improving.

173
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:15,720
I'll direct traffic,
so you two contact the station.

174
00:11:16,140 --> 00:11:16,820
Understood.

175
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:26,360
Senpai

176
00:11:28,120 --> 00:11:30,600
Fortunately,
the injuries aren't serious, apparently.

177
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:31,940
I see. That's good.

178
00:11:38,700 --> 00:11:40,480
So you're still alive

179
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:41,640
Die.

180
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:44,360
I'm heading out on patrol.

181
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,620
Good work.

182
00:11:56,860 --> 00:11:59,480
Hey, that car is speeding!

183
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:02,360
Stop! Won't you stop?!

184
00:12:09,100 --> 00:12:11,620
What? What's that mark?

185
00:12:16,780 --> 00:12:18,920
Watanuki, is that you, Watanuki?

186
00:12:19,320 --> 00:12:22,570
Heh heh, looks like you didn't forget,

187
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:24,820
my old friend from the Black Meteor days!

188
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,960
I'm back in Japan after all this time.

189
00:12:28,960 --> 00:12:31,960
To get revenge on you, the traitor.

190
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:33,980
What are you doing?

191
00:12:33,980 --> 00:12:37,960
Caron! The black blood in my eyes
won't tolerate traffic violations!

192
00:12:37,960 --> 00:12:38,980
We'll see about that.

193
00:12:38,980 --> 00:12:39,560
What?

194
00:12:39,560 --> 00:12:42,940
Did you think I wouldn't know your weakness?

195
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:44,680
My weakness?

196
00:12:46,780 --> 00:12:48,300
I know it, you know.

197
00:12:48,300 --> 00:12:51,820
That you swore to wipe out traffic
violations with that police light.

198
00:12:53,400 --> 00:12:54,120
What do you mean?

199
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:54,400
Don't!

200
00:12:58,540 --> 00:12:59,460
What are you doing!

201
00:13:05,480 --> 00:13:07,040
I'm losing strength.

202
00:13:10,580 --> 00:13:13,620
Just as I thought!
I'm taking this one with me!

203
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:16,021
From now on, I'll break traffic laws,

204
00:13:16,071 --> 00:13:18,180
break them, and break them all the way!

205
00:13:37,340 --> 00:13:37,740
What?

206
00:13:38,500 --> 00:13:41,040
Chief Ohara's patrol light was stolen?

207
00:13:41,740 --> 00:13:43,640
The patrol light from that vow?

208
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:46,120
Do you know who did it?

209
00:13:47,620 --> 00:13:50,840
It's a man named Watanuki, an old
motorcycle buddy from his days riding.

210
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:56,140
He's the one who came up
in Chief Ohara's story.

211
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:59,540
He was the vice-leader of the Black Meteor.

212
00:14:00,620 --> 00:14:02,120
And what about Chief Ohara?

213
00:14:02,780 --> 00:14:05,760
He's completely lost all motivation.

214
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,460
He's been like that ever since.

215
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:18,500
It's even throwing us off.

216
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:20,460
He must have been really shocked.

217
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:23,700
Let's cheer him up a bit.

218
00:14:24,580 --> 00:14:26,960
Well, well, Chief Ohara.

219
00:14:29,240 --> 00:14:30,480
Chief Ohara!

220
00:14:31,380 --> 00:14:32,860
It's you.

221
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:36,720
Come on, pull yourself together.

222
00:14:36,720 --> 00:14:38,860
Just because your patrol light was stolen...

223
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:41,820
I told you about it, didn't I?

224
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:45,980
That patrol light was a sworn oath to me.

225
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:49,880
Now that it's gone,
I've lost all my drive and everything.

226
00:14:50,980 --> 00:14:55,160
Then who's going to lead the
traffic safety guidance from now on?

227
00:14:55,820 --> 00:14:58,580
I'll leave it to you young ones.

228
00:14:58,580 --> 00:15:00,840
I'm retiring.

229
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:03,180
Chief Ohara.

230
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:12,920
What's going on?

231
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:26,480
Isn't that the patrol
light stolen from the Chief?

232
00:15:28,640 --> 00:15:29,660
Well, how interesting!

233
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:37,720
Don't think you can outrun a big Honda.

234
00:15:37,720 --> 00:15:42,040
You're just a lowly box officer,
so don't act so high and mighty!

235
00:15:42,500 --> 00:15:43,300
What did you say?

236
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:44,920
Traffic violations, my foot!

237
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:46,420
Death Rider.

238
00:15:46,960 --> 00:15:47,560
Hold on.

239
00:15:48,220 --> 00:15:49,220
It's a quiz!

240
00:15:49,220 --> 00:15:51,120
Green light means go.

241
00:15:51,120 --> 00:15:52,820
Then what about red lights?

242
00:15:52,820 --> 00:15:53,880
Stop.

243
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:54,540
Stop.

244
00:15:54,540 --> 00:15:56,860
Ignoring that is my reason for living.

245
00:16:20,540 --> 00:16:22,140
Wait, Chief Ohara.

246
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,380
We know who the culprit is.

247
00:16:24,380 --> 00:16:27,280
Let's go catch Watanuki together.

248
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:29,720
Come on, Chief Ohara.

249
00:16:30,620 --> 00:16:31,580
Chief Ohara.

250
00:16:36,400 --> 00:16:40,100
Damn it,
I'm not old enough to be washed up yet.

251
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:41,060
That's right.

252
00:16:41,060 --> 00:16:44,300
This is your fault for
not catching him properly.

253
00:16:44,300 --> 00:16:47,680
That guy's motorcycle skills are incredible.

254
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:51,580
The only one who can match him
is Chief Ohara when he's serious.

255
00:16:52,140 --> 00:16:55,260
And Chief Ohara already thinks he's retired.

256
00:16:55,260 --> 00:16:57,700
I guess we'll just have to
crack down the old-fashioned way.

257
00:17:04,680 --> 00:17:06,960
I'll make a ruckus again tonight.

258
00:17:12,720 --> 00:17:13,640
Out of the way, out of the way!

259
00:17:17,660 --> 00:17:20,720
I'm not bound by traffic
regulations like this!

260
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:26,280
Spotted a rear overtake! Pursuing!

261
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:33,920
Apparently the black
shooting star has appeared!

262
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,040
Right, we're going after him too!

263
00:17:41,280 --> 00:17:44,020
Looks like there are lots
of patrol cars out tonight.

264
00:17:44,420 --> 00:17:46,680
The black shooting star must have appeared.

265
00:17:46,680 --> 00:17:49,460
That's the one who stole
Dad's patrol light, right?

266
00:17:51,480 --> 00:17:52,520
No parking!

267
00:17:54,360 --> 00:17:55,900
Aren't you going out on patrol, Dad?

268
00:17:56,240 --> 00:18:00,120
Your job is to catch bad people who break traffic laws,
isn't it?

269
00:18:00,200 --> 00:18:02,960
Don't talk, just eat!

270
00:18:04,300 --> 00:18:06,650
I've already left it
to the younger officers.

271
00:18:06,700 --> 00:18:08,500
Dad's retired, you know.

272
00:18:12,980 --> 00:18:15,140
If you can catch me, then try!

273
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:19,880
Watanuki! This isn't an escape route!

274
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:22,020
Surrender quietly and
let yourself be tied up!

275
00:18:22,020 --> 00:18:24,420
I wonder about that?

276
00:18:32,340 --> 00:18:36,000
I can't be tied down unless
I lay down the rules first.

277
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,640
Hey! It's on!

278
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:44,600
What a crazy old geezer.

279
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:48,860
Looks like we're pretty close.

280
00:18:56,080 --> 00:18:59,880
A happy family,
built by betraying your comrades

281
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:08,280
Stop!

282
00:19:13,060 --> 00:19:14,840
Oh my God, what have I done?

283
00:19:19,840 --> 00:19:21,260
Chief Ohara

284
00:19:22,020 --> 00:19:22,740
Are you hurt?

285
00:19:23,420 --> 00:19:24,300
I'm fine.

286
00:19:24,760 --> 00:19:25,860
Good, that's a relief.

287
00:19:26,520 --> 00:19:30,420
Chief Ohara, why are you staying
silent after they've gone this far?

288
00:19:30,820 --> 00:19:33,260
But without that patrol light,

289
00:19:33,260 --> 00:19:37,020
you can still crack down on traffic violations without that thing,
can't you?

290
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:38,880
Dad, this.

291
00:19:40,460 --> 00:19:41,340
W-what's this?

292
00:19:41,940 --> 00:19:46,760
You seemed so lonely without your patrol light,
so I tried making one.

293
00:19:46,760 --> 00:19:48,620
I didn't make it very well, though.

294
00:19:48,620 --> 00:19:50,600
It's really badly made, isn't it.

295
00:19:52,020 --> 00:19:54,820
But it's pretty well made. Thanks.

296
00:19:57,680 --> 00:20:01,420
Now the patrol light in my heart is lit up!

297
00:20:15,480 --> 00:20:19,040
Called the walking traffic law for 35 years.

298
00:20:19,040 --> 00:20:21,680
Traffic Safety Instruction Master, Part 7.

299
00:20:21,680 --> 00:20:24,360
Ishizuru Tetsu wo Kenzan.

300
00:20:26,320 --> 00:20:31,140
Damn you! Today I'll bring the iron hammer
of justice down on the black shooting star.

301
00:20:31,140 --> 00:20:37,400
Why are you driving so slowly?

302
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:39,500
Exactly 40 kilometers an hour, isn't it?

303
00:20:40,360 --> 00:20:42,840
Hey, at this speed, they'll get away!

304
00:20:43,660 --> 00:20:46,480
The speed limit on this road
is 40 kilometers an hour.

305
00:20:46,480 --> 00:20:48,900
We're chasing a criminal,
so that's fine, right?

306
00:20:49,360 --> 00:20:52,920
No way.
At all times, traffic safety comes first.

307
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:59,080
There you are again, Ishizu!

308
00:20:59,260 --> 00:21:02,160
But you'll never catch me!

309
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:03,620
I won't let you get away!

310
00:21:06,420 --> 00:21:08,920
What? Got him! I caught you!

311
00:21:09,360 --> 00:21:10,900
I'll drag you down!

312
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:14,300
Here we go!

313
00:21:14,840 --> 00:21:17,440
Stop! This road has a 40 km speed limit!

314
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:20,260
Breaking that is my whole reason for living!

315
00:21:22,160 --> 00:21:22,960
Whoa!

316
00:21:23,020 --> 00:21:24,140
Stop it!

317
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:25,480
Watanuki!

318
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:28,860
What are you doing?! We're going after him!

319
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:31,240
But the speed limit is...

320
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:33,180
You mean...

321
00:21:33,600 --> 00:21:34,960
Whoa! What are you doing?

322
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:36,660
We're speeding up!

323
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:39,020
Stop! This is a 40 km/h zone!

324
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:39,820
Go, go!

325
00:21:41,400 --> 00:21:45,160
If you speed up any more,
I'm going over 60 kilometers an hour!

326
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:54,660
Yes! Chief Ohara has lost his restraint!

327
00:21:57,360 --> 00:21:58,700
Watanuki!

328
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:02,340
Just give back the patrol light, damn you!

329
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:05,800
Finally getting serious, are you, Ohara!

330
00:22:06,180 --> 00:22:07,660
Don't you dare tell me to shut up!

331
00:22:10,040 --> 00:22:11,060
The bastard actually did it!

332
00:22:15,380 --> 00:22:16,560
Help me!

333
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:29,160
Where on earth are you going?!

334
00:22:29,560 --> 00:22:32,980
This is a world we can't
possibly keep up with.

335
00:22:32,980 --> 00:22:36,720
Just as expected of Traffic
Safety Instructor Master Nanadamu.

336
00:22:40,860 --> 00:22:43,480
So, did you end up
catching him on Sado Island?

337
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:47,640
I don't even remember
crossing the sea myself.

338
00:22:47,640 --> 00:22:49,220
That must have been rough.

339
00:22:49,220 --> 00:22:52,240
It's terrible! Chief Ohara's...

340
00:22:52,240 --> 00:22:54,300
Did something else happen?

341
00:22:54,860 --> 00:22:55,520
Well, it's...

342
00:22:59,340 --> 00:23:00,140
W-what is this...

343
00:23:00,840 --> 00:23:03,300
It's like Chief Ohara's home, isn't it?

344
00:23:03,300 --> 00:23:05,360
Did Chief Ohara do this?

345
00:23:05,800 --> 00:23:06,200
Yes.

346
00:23:06,660 --> 00:23:08,760
Hey, Kankichi Ryotsu!

347
00:23:08,760 --> 00:23:11,020
What did you do to Chief Ohara?

348
00:23:11,020 --> 00:23:12,660
I didn't do anything!

349
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:18,000
Chief Ohara got all fired up first thing this morning and trashed the room like this,
on top of that,

350
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:21,700
he went and changed everyone's names in
the Traffic Division without permission!

351
00:23:21,700 --> 00:23:24,800
He said my name is now "Seisho School Zone"!

352
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:26,760
Naoko got off easy.

353
00:23:26,760 --> 00:23:29,380
Me? I'm Ono Rakuseki, number ten!

354
00:23:30,320 --> 00:23:33,740
By the way, I'm Reiko Akimoto.

355
00:23:34,920 --> 00:23:36,380
Here they come.

356
00:23:36,800 --> 00:23:40,420
No Motorcycles or Mopeds Allowed.

357
00:23:41,180 --> 00:23:43,760
Could that possibly be my name?

358
00:23:43,760 --> 00:23:45,360
Yeah, that's nice, isn't it?

359
00:23:45,360 --> 00:23:47,960
Everyone, change quickly and assemble.

360
00:23:47,960 --> 00:23:50,820
We will now hold a traffic safety lecture.

361
00:23:52,200 --> 00:23:54,240
Traffic safety lecture.

362
00:23:54,780 --> 00:23:56,880
Please, anything but that.

363
00:23:57,760 --> 00:23:58,760
Don't run away!

364
00:23:58,760 --> 00:24:01,140
Cars can't stop suddenly.

365
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:20,460
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

366
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:27,120
Walking while looking back,
holding Mom's hand

367
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:34,260
That strange feeling I had back then

368
00:24:35,460 --> 00:24:39,540
So I walked along the arcade's tiles

369
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:45,300
stepping only on the black ones

370
00:24:47,820 --> 00:24:53,580
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten

371
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:57,620
Politicians with their pompous faces,

372
00:24:57,620 --> 00:25:00,920
and the aunties who are a thorn in your side

373
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:06,520
Turn that corner, come on

374
00:25:07,460 --> 00:25:11,740
You can meet everyone, everyone

375
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:19,680
There's a wall over
there surely there's a wall

376
00:25:20,900 --> 00:25:24,900
Everyone, come on, to our town

377
00:25:25,720 --> 00:25:26,480
Thank you

378
00:25:30,920 --> 00:25:32,320
Do you know what a trolleybus is?

379
00:25:32,600 --> 00:25:34,880
It takes electricity from
overhead wires and runs on the road

380
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:37,540
It's a vehicle like a
combination of a train and a bus

381
00:25:37,540 --> 00:25:40,140
When I was a kid,
there were lots of them running around

382
00:25:40,720 --> 00:25:43,700
And I have an unforgettable
memory of the trolleybus

383
00:25:44,080 --> 00:25:47,040
Next time,
the Trolleybus Story, see you then

384
00:25:59,360 --> 00:26:00,760
Thank you

